    "created_at": "2015-11-12T08:30:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-11-12T08:30:49Z",
    "body": "Ideally, if it's not specified, it's not allowed. But there's still quite a bit of handwaving the lower on the stack you go. Servers seem to rely on clients behaving in a certain way. I'm sure they're not going to be happy if we start sending them these headers without optin.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
