    "created_at": "2016-05-27T16:47:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-27T16:47:53Z",
    "body": "Even without the teeing optimization, supporting Expect: 100-continue could be useful for large requests, in particular file uploads. The server may be able to respond immediately with an error (like a 401 or 403), meaning that clients for whom network usage is important (mobile in particular) can avoid wasting network on a request whose body will be ignored.\n",
